# Adds the CMake build system (CMakeLists.txt, defs.cmake, cmake/*.cmake,
# get_quickjs.cmake.in, quickjs-config.cmake.in) as an alternative to the
# stock Makefile: builds qjs/qjsc/libquickjs(.so|.a), generates
# quickjs-config.h via configure_file(), and optionally pulls in sibling
# qjs-* module subdirectories (qjs-ffi, qjs-modules, qjs-debugger, ...) if
# present -- see MODULE_* options in CMakeLists.txt.
#
# Regenerated from the current tree: the cmake system now takes its helper
# functions from the qjs-modules submodule (qjs-modules/cmake/Functions.cmake,
# Checks.cmake and Compat.cmake) instead of a local cmake/functions.cmake,
# so qjs-modules must be checked out next to it. Configure output is a short
# set of tables (message_table); module subdirectories only show warnings
# unless -DQUICKJS_VERBOSE_MODULES=ON. New options:
#   * QUICKJS_DEBUGGER (ON)   - build quickjs-debugger*.c and enable the
#     hooks in quickjs.c (renamed from CONFIG_DEBUGGER); qjs-debugger is
#     skipped when it is off.
#   * CONFIG_FIND_MODULE (ON) - build quickjs-find-module.c and let qjs/qjsc
#     resolve bare module names on the module search path.
#
# Apply after patches/001, 002 and 004 (003 doesn't apply to
# quickjs-2026-06-04 -- see its own header). Three small companion hunks
# in quickjs.c/qjs.c/qjsc.c add '#ifdef HAVE_QUICKJS_CONFIG_H / #include
# "quickjs-config.h" / #endif' next to their other includes -- without
# this the CMake-generated config header (CONFIG_VERSION, CONFIG_SHEXT,
# QUICKJS_MODULE_PATH, ...) never reaches the source and things like
# CONFIG_VERSION in JS_DumpMemoryUsage() fail to compile.
#
# Adapted for quickjs-2026-06-04's source layout vs. what this fork's
# defs.cmake originally assumed (a 2024-01-13 tree):
#   * libbf.c/libbf.h -> dtoa.c/dtoa.h (CONFIG_BIGNUM/libbf was dropped
#     upstream in favor of dtoa.c; defs.cmake now picks whichever of the
#     two is actually present in QUICKJS_SOURCES_ROOT).
#   * win32-poll.c is only added to QUICKJS_SOURCES if it exists (only
#     true when patches/003-poll.patch also applied -- it doesn't on
#     2026-06-04, see that patch's header).
#   * qjscalc.c generation/build/install-symlink in CMakeLists.txt is
#     gated on qjscalc.js existing (removed upstream along with the
#     bignum calculator; QJSCALC_SOURCES is empty and everything
#     downstream of it is skipped when it's absent).
#
# Originally verified end-to-end against quickjs-2026-06-04 with patches
# 001+002+004 applied: cmake -S . -B build && cmake --build build
# succeeds (qjs, qjsc, libquickjs.so), `qjs --help` reports
# "QuickJS version 2026-06-04", `qjs -e '1+2'`-style eval works, and
# `QUICKJS_MODULE_PATH=... qjs -m` resolves a bare module specifier
# through quickjs-find-module.c (patch 002).
#
